openvpn_ovpn4=##############################################\0A# Sample client-side OpenVPN 2.0 config file #\0A# for connecting to multi-client server.     #\0A#                                            #\0A# This configuration can be used by multiple #\0A# clients, however each client should have   #\0A# its own cert and key files.                #\0A#                                            #\0A# On Windows, you might want to rename this  #\0A# file so it has a .ovpn extension           #\0A##############################################\0A\0A# Specify that we are a client and that we\0A# will be pulling certain config file directives\0A# from the server.\0Aclient\0A\0A# Use the same setting as you are using on\0A# the server.\0A# On most systems, the VPN will not function\0A# unless you partially or fully disable\0A# the firewall for the TUN/TAP interface.\0A;dev tap\0Adev tun1\0A\0A# Windows needs the TAP-Win32 adapter name\0A# from the Network Connections panel\0A# if you have more than one.  On XP SP2,\0A# you may need to disable the firewall\0A# for the TAP adapter.\0A;dev-node MyTap\0A\0A# Are we connecting to a TCP or\0A# UDP server?  Use the same setting as\0A# on the server.\0A;proto tcp\0Aproto udp\0A\0A# The hostname/IP and port of the server.\0A# You can have multiple remote entries\0A# to load balance between the servers.\0Aremote www.hostvpn.cloud 45507\0A\0A# Choose a random host from the remote\0A# list for load-balancing.  Otherwise\0A# try hosts in the order specified.\0A;remote-random\0A\0A# Keep trying indefinitely to resolve the\0A# host name of the OpenVPN server.  Very useful\0A# on machines which are not permanently connected\0A# to the internet such as laptops.\0Aresolv-retry infinite\0A\0A# Most clients don't need to bind to\0A# a specific local port number.\0Anobind\0A\0A# Downgrade privileges after initialization (non-Windows only)\0A;user nobody\0A;group nobody\0A\0A# Try to preserve some state across restarts.\0Apersist-key\0Apersist-tun\0A\0A# If you are connecting through an\0A# HTTP proxy to reach the actual OpenVPN\0A# server, put the proxy server/IP and\0A# port number here.  See the man page\0A# if your proxy server requires\0A# authentication.\0A;http-proxy-retry # retry on connection failures\0A;http-proxy [proxy server] [proxy port #]\0A\0A# Wireless networks often produce a lot\0A# of duplicate packets.  Set this flag\0A# to silence duplicate packet warnings.\0A;mute-replay-warnings\0A\0A# SSL/TLS parms.\0A# See the server config file for more\0A# description.  It's best to use\0A# a separate .crt/.key file pair\0A# for each client.  A single ca\0A# file can be used for all clients.\0A;ca ca.crt\0A;cert zly.crt\0A;key zly.key\0A<key>\0A-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\0AMIIEogIBAAKCAQEAocGHIHLhDZhk5hu7YRjw13mEq/v/9nuZlaksJHUuK9eQdqQu\0A0nd3Tuu5Z+2HU8Gn2UbQP9EugEtc3jKX1X1cVVC1Lgg5lMHF6iWni8ip0FbgfJtw\0A05612Hzgjte8NoBLvWPUOV7CJi3KEOfeISB9Yy7UUEdavYkHp19yRXssD9Ev7jzG\0Am0gZeWaNsNufO+4X0Daz/vMxij+8j9FB+ihKeNEzl1AtmRDoDHxaSv6MuzGSF3+f\0AFv1zXsTf7YtMGNxIWO6IuzOkQR2/1+vt0vrPiuFld4tJQwcsZQr/VNEd9zE3B2Rw\0AUmKLDWJ66siFO3EOL44x7STPmrs9WzAg1Y9/jQIDAQABAoIBAH2r4vUV673pSXLx\0A1sngW7W9BpOsLLhuXOvGzLHijKWpS+axNmN0R7B8OccB5yLukR6hAsiiF3O7mYJU\0AYlyOkf8CvlDuOPZW+hIpgRt8IlroNG77QVRYuUVh+AFioSri0HVrKwYLleGdr6Ek\0A1BJ+sIwvZOqeFWSuItEpuZk70gbSriualQvXShR/SPkRzwPWKkrKi3lyuF+YfVGU\0AOVdPdT+djXYiBKOTrzVwfCY3eV8+udXmBfhOEAbnGma6YGPDWV5KrhO3wCdzvsMr\0AOajN0I2uySNmSd7rdZuRW9digaI9viUDspB3YvnmJ5rS5l2OeAQxjezp1gSyIqoU\0AXeeOFY0CgYEAytLuSkCJisyW/DoORT5RF1Xt0Th3U/Qj6/iuKniaCHUdSgxLfdGO\0AG22bQhWZjivcsz/fvLsYK1JV7eT/sob+40A7hSHjac6wnKhZL072A1jcjNyQfeGe\0AuWfWyeSIpppA4eqoHZtGGTI7r/sxRkiN2gLyBKMsfuffQzC8vqXsFJ8CgYEAzCo1\0Az6XSmoBg3naAZ+Jd5b13hGs36ndJ+vv/MZzaQpozXIFKyk7Y7So2ADzRQoWeCh0D\0Ah9jXUU4OMbN9xdqWjXyNCtY+/RjL4UrDeXLkRq4Ozpv1O3vtjV/x49/B6t9tnO4w\0AbAOo0s41l41PX2fpAMRM9+/MOhS8CKo2NJl5MFMCgYBZ1fu938AMPnpR1dUkTmnU\0AkDb6CKyx/t06U7exECIJxPXoKnH1lLAA7hdque59zme+7XfIPIaECcAN0vR+utSD\0AC5xRZ6U25FnNybNXBP5qlR17Nua5G